## ⚡ Quick test
1. Refunds `{{last_tran_id}}` by `{{refund_amount}}`. RSA encryption runs inside this collection with no package download; if secure randomness is unavailable, set `{{refund_merchant_auth}}` manually and retry.
2. After a successful refund, re-send **3. Check Transaction** — status becomes `4 (REFUNDED)`.

## Refund
RSA payload: `{ "mc_id": "...", "tran_id": "...", "refund_amount": "..." }`
Hash: `request_time + merchant_id + merchant_auth` (merchant_auth is the **base64 of the RSA-encrypted** payload).

**Secure randomness unavailable?** Pre-encrypt and paste into `{{refund_merchant_auth}}` (old-style `openssl_public_encrypt`); the script will use it automatically.

```php
$data = json_encode(['mc_id'=>$mcId,'tran_id'=>$tranId,'refund_amount'=>number_format($amount,2,'.','')]);
openssl_public_encrypt($data, $encrypted, $pubKey, OPENSSL_PKCS1_PADDING);
$merchant_auth = base64_encode($encrypted);
$hash = base64_encode(hash_hmac('sha512', $requestTime.$mcId.$merchant_auth, $secretKey, true));
```

